      <floats-group id="article-28799.s16">
        <fig id="article-28799.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Seabather&#x02019;s Eruption. This patient developed an intensely pruritic rash with erythematous papules and vesicles, primarily in areas covered by swimwear, approximately 12 hours after larval exposure, with typical distribution on the buttocks and lower torso. The condition is most commonly caused by larval <italic toggle="yes">Linuche unguiculata</italic> (thimble jellyfish) or <italic toggle="yes">Edwardsiella lineata</italic> (sea anemone). Jpatokal, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seabathers_eruption.jpg">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Seabathers_eruption" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
